CMJ metadata should be available through hidden include paths.

  $ . ./setup.sh
  $ mkdir hidden public
  $ echo 'let add3 a b c = a + b + c' > hidden/lib.ml
  $ melc hidden/lib.ml -o hidden/lib.js
  $ cp hidden/lib.cmi public/
  $ echo 'let () = Js.log (Lib.add3 1 2 3)' > main.ml

  $ melc -I public -H hidden --mel-stop-after-cmj main.ml
  $ melc -I hidden --mel-module-type es6 main.cmj -o main.js
  $ cat main.js
  // Generated by Melange
  
  import * as Curry from "melange.js/curry.js";
  import * as Lib from "./hidden/lib.js";
  
  console.log(Curry._3(Lib.add3, 1, 2, 3));
  /*  Not a pure module */

Making the CMJ visible recovers the function's arity.

  $ melc -I hidden --mel-stop-after-cmj main.ml
  $ melc -I hidden --mel-module-type es6 main.cmj -o main.js
  $ cat main.js
  // Generated by Melange
  
  import * as Lib from "./hidden/lib.js";
  
  console.log(Lib.add3(1, 2, 3));
  /*  Not a pure module */
